# A string constant is written into the emitted module as a line of its own,
# and the pass that drops `tailcc` from calls that do not need it read every
# line of that module. So a program printing the words `call tailcc` lost them
# from the constant and kept its declared length, and clang refused the module:
# the interpreter printed this sample and the compiler could not build it. The
# pass now leaves every global's line alone, and the strings below spell each
# word it looks for.
pub play =
  print "call tailcc here"
  >> print "musttail call tailcc @f(i64 1)"
  >> print "define tailcc %KValue @g("
